hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2962","**\nNarrated to us Abdullah ibn Sa‘id al-Ashajj (RA),\nNarrated to us Ibn Numayr (RA).\nAnd narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Khashram (RA), he informed us ‘Isa (RA).\nAnd narrated to us Salam ibn Junadah (RA), narrated to us Abu Mu‘awiyah (RA).\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar (RA), narrated to us ‘Abd al-Rahman (RA), narrated to us Sufyan (RA).\nAnd narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa (RA), narrated to us Abu Mu‘awiyah (RA) and Jarir (RA), all of them from al-A‘mash (RA), except that in the hadith of al-Thawri (RA) from Sulayman (i.e., al-A‘mash) from Ibrahim from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid (RA), he said:\n\n“Uthman (RA) prayed four rak‘ahs at Mina. So Abdullah (RA) said, ‘I prayed two rak‘ahs with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), two rak‘ahs with Abu Bakr (RA), and two rak‘ahs with ‘Umar (RA). Then the paths diverged with you. I wish I had two accepted rak‘ahs out of these four.’”\n\nThis is the wording of Salam ibn Junadah’s hadith."
"2963","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Al-Ala', who said: Narrated to us Abu Khalid, on the authority of Ubaydullah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn Umar (RA), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," Abu Bakr (RA)"," and Umar (RA) prayed two Rak'ahs at Mina"," and Uthman (RA) did so during the early part of his caliphate.\"""""
